<%#
  A Highcharts chart, with its height **reserved before it renders**.

  The container used to be an empty div, so it was 0px tall until Highcharts inflated it on
  `connect()` -- and everything under it, the two buttons and the whole table card, was thrown
  850px down the page a moment after the reader could already see it. Measured with Chrome's own
  `layout-shift` entries: **CLS 0.352** on all three historical trend pages, against thresholds of
  0.1 good and 0.25 poor. It was the worst layout shift in the app by an order of magnitude.

  Reserving the box is Chrome's own advice for anything that arrives late -- the same reason an
  `<img>` carries width and height. The height comes from the caller rather than from parsing the
  config back out of its JSON, so the number the box reserves and the number the chart draws at
  cannot disagree.
%>
<div data-controller="highchart" data-highchart-config-value="<%= config %>">
  <div data-highchart-target="chart" style="min-height: <%= height %>px"></div>
  <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
    <button type="button" class="<%= essentials_button_classes(variant: :secondary, size: :sm) %>"
            data-action="click->highchart#selectAll">Select all</button>
    <button type="button" class="<%= essentials_button_classes(variant: :secondary, size: :sm) %>"
            data-action="click->highchart#deselectAll">Deselect all</button>
  </div>
</div>
